Z||000000||fropuff||07-15-2001||01:54 AM||||Hey guys.  Up here in the great wilderness of Minnesota, we have the great opportunity to use front license plates on our vehicles.  When I get my new front fascia painted, I'm going to put some projector fog lamps in.  I hate the look of front plates on Fieros, and I've already Bondo-d over the small bracket marks.  I was wondering if you can put the license plate on dash board, showing through the windshield--kinda like you see on the ghetto cruisers.  If I can, I'd mount the plate on a piece of plastic.  I was going to not put it on until I get pulled over by the friendly neighborhood po-leece, but I don't need to get b*tched at anymore than I have to.  I also want to put a cover on the rear plates, which are illegal, and I don't need any trouble.  Thanks!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Standard||07-15-2001||02:06 AM||||Well, I don't have a front plate on my coupe right now.. if I get pulled over for it I'm gonna unleash the "it didn't have a bracket when i got it, and they don't make them anymore" spiel.  Or the "it broke and I can't find a replacement for it".   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">        <BR>1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed<P><FONT SIZE="1">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto<BR><FONT COLOR="red">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroKyle||07-15-2001||02:10 AM||||in the great state of michigan we don't have to worry about such issues, I take the front plate for granted||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jaei Sun||07-15-2001||02:21 AM||||Last weekend I got pulled over on University and was cited "Obstructed Front Plate".  Tho I'm going to fight it cuz I don't have a front licence bracket, car didn't come with one, and I had the plate behind the aero nose holes... you can still see the plate and read it head on.  ||||reg||8
